SwiftPutty local patch 0010
Upstream: PuTTY 0.85 (a3cce3a48d4ab12e0fccb32998b9042d4f7c3ff1)
Status:   reported upstream (2026-10-19); should be (a proxy connection can hang)

HTTP proxy: complete the blank line that ends the response headers at
once.

read_line() treats a header line as complete only when the byte after
its newline arrives, so that it can tell whether the next line is a
continuation (starting with a space or tab). That is right for real
header lines, but it also applied to the empty line ending the header
section. When the proxy sends nothing after that line, the negotiation
stalls:

  - a "407 Proxy Authentication Required" with "Content-Length: 0":
    the authenticated retry waits until the proxy sends more, and
  - a "200 Connection established": the tunnel is not handed to the
    backend until the destination sends a byte, so protocols where the
    client speaks first (Rlogin, Raw) never start.

Found with an HTTP proxy played by Core/tests/spb_backends_test.c. An
empty line cannot be continued, so it is complete as soon as its
newline arrives.

--- a/proxy/http.c
+++ b/proxy/http.c
@@ -30,6 +30,17 @@
                  * header, then any newline terminates it. */
                 goto done;
             }
+
+            if (is_header && output->s[output->len - 1] == '\n' &&
+                (output->len == 1 ||
+                 (output->len == 2 && output->s[0] == '\r'))) {
+                /* An empty line ends the header section, and cannot
+                 * be continued: it is complete now. Waiting for the
+                 * next byte would stall whenever the proxy sends
+                 * nothing more (a 407 with no body, or a 200 before
+                 * the server's first byte). */
+                goto done;
+            }
         }
     }
 
